# Gitignored, dev-box-only (has a local DATABASE_URL + dev secrets in [env]).
# Empirically confirmed (2026-07-29): if this leaks into the build context on
# a dev box that has it on disk, cargo's sqlx macros pick up its DATABASE_URL
# and try a LIVE connection during `cargo build --release`, which fails
# (Connection refused, no Postgres reachable from the build container) instead
# of using the committed .sqlx offline cache. A fresh CI checkout never has
# this file (it's gitignored), so this only bites local `docker build` runs --
# excluded here so local builds match CI behavior. Belt-and-suspenders with
# Dockerfile.server's `ENV SQLX_OFFLINE=true`, which is the real fix.
.cargo/
